      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{65e53dfbf897545663236251|full_name} Try disabling IPV6 in your network settings, it solved the problem for me a couple minutes ago. \n\nControl Panel\n\nNetwork and Internet\n\nNetwork and sharing center\n\nwhere it says connections: Ethernet \n\nclick on ethernet\n\nclick on properties\n\ndisable Internet Protocol version 6 (TCP/IPv6)\n\nYou shouldn't have to restart your computer\n\nhopefully that solves it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
